  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 124 PM CDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nThe streak of hot days is expected to continue through the weekend \nand into next week. Thursday may be the hottest day of the week by a \nslim margin with LREF mean 700mb temperatures aloft reaching 14C, or \naround the 98th percentile for much of the area. Daytime winds \nshould remain on the breezier side through Friday. A temporary \nincrease in moisture from the Gulf is anticipated Friday, but stable \nconditions due to the overarching presence of ridging keeps rain \nchances low, providing little aside from than prolonging high heat \nindices. We'll continue to monitor for the need to issue a Heat \nAdvisory if one of these days becomes notably hotter than our recent \nstreak of conditions, but reliable access to cooling and hydration \nwill be needed regardless of whether those levels are met.\n\nThe mid level Gulf ridge slides into the lower Mississippi Valley\nover the weekend, but will then expand west into the Southern \nPlains early next week. This progression is well represented in \nensembles and is a sign that hot summer conditions will continue \nwith only minor fluctuations in air temperature and heat indices \neach day. Highs should stay in the upper 90s to low 100s while \novernight lows should continue to stay in the mid to upper 70s for\nmost. The northward jaunt of the ridge over the weekend could \ntemporarily spruce up southeasterly flow just enough to allow a \nfew isolated seabreeze showers to get going again over the Coastal\nPlains, but otherwise rain chances remain minimal through mid- \nAugust.",
